[0.085, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mWrite\u001b[22m(~/project\u001b[19G/manifest/build/commit-w12s3b.txt)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mWrote \u001b[1m12\u001b[15G\u001b[22mlines to \u001b[1m~/projects/manifest/build/commit-w12s3b.txt\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 1 \u001b[22mProcurement: th\u001b[26G issuer's \u001b[37Gark\u001b[41Gt rules k\u001b[52Gt, W12 slice 3\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m \u001b[9G \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  3 \u001b[22mSlice 3's gate measured the console's Ore to Brine at 4.29 s against its\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  4 \u001b[22m3.56 s budget: on every economic turn's last step the AI issuer called\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  5 \u001b[22mTrade::Reliefs, which worked out the market's rules from the content again,\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  6 \u001b[22mas Trade::TenderPrice's shortcut said it would until a profile showed it.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  7 \u001b[22mTrade::MakePricer keeps them, as MakeBuyer does, and the issuer prices and\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  8 \u001b[22mcalls its reliefs through it; the free functions stay, the procurement suite\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 9 \u001b[22mholding the two to\u001b[29Gthe same budgets. Ore to Brine\u001b[60Gis 3.46 to 3.48\u001b[76Gs in\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m0 \u001b[22mRelease, as \u001b[23Gt 7302d83 before W12 (3.46\u001b[50Gand 3.47).\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m… +2 lines \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BComm\u001b[8Gtted \u001b[1maa4b4e3\u001b[22m, searching for \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m pattern, running \u001b[1m5\u001b[22m shell\u001b[63Gcommands…\r\u001b[80C\u001b[3B\u001b[K\r\u001b[18C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m1h 2m 15s · ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m104.8k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[18C\u001b[6B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(shift+tab to cycle) · esc to int