[0.015, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m3\u001b[14G\u001b[22mlines, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[36G\u001b[K\r\u001b[9C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m0\u001b[16G\u001b[22msave's new compon\u001b[34Gnt alon\u001b[42G,\u001b[44Gits fast-forward's calls uncha\u001b[75Gged. Left:\u001b[86Ga rel\u001b[92Gef\u001b[95Gtender a player's\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 1251 \u001b[22m    governor publishes, which `Publish` does not take. The issuer keeps the market's rules\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 1252 \u001b[22m    (`Trade::MakePricer`, after slice 3's gate measured the console's Ore to Brine at 4.29 s against\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 1253 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m   its 3.56 s budget when each turn's call rebuilt them): 3.46 to 3.48 s, as before W12.             \r\u001b[9C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m3\u001b[16G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mits 3.56\u001b[25Gs budget when each turn's\u001b[51Gcall rebuilt th\u001b[67Gm): 3.46\u001b[76Gto\u001b[79G3.48\u001b[84Gs,\u001b[87Gas\u001b[90Gbefore\u001b[97GW12.\u001b[48;2;4;71;0m That budget\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 1254 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m   was L27's 2.37 s with half as much again, which the economy since had nearly used up, so it was   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 1255 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m   measured again after slice 3: 3.50 s, failing above 5.25 s.                                       \r\u001b[9C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m6\u001b[13G\u001b[22m3.\u001b[16GBids and the\u001b[29Gaw\u001b[32Grd: \u001b[37Gealed bids, rev\u001b[53Gsions,\u001b[60Gwithdrawal\u001b[72Gthe tie order, the bond's\u001b[98Gfallback and\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 1257 \u001b[16G\u001b[22msimultaneous\u001b[29Gawards\u001b[36Gcompeting\u001b[46Gfor\u001b[50Gfunds;\u001b[57G`Closed`\u001b[66Gat\u001b[69Gthe\u001b[73Gboundary.\u001b[83